# Next.js Frontend Rule

- Prefer server components by default; add client components only when needed for interactivity/browser APIs.
- Keep UI components presentational and move business logic into hooks or `lib` utilities.
- Reuse existing design patterns and utility styles before adding new variants.
- Validate loading/error/empty states for new async UI flows.
- Preserve route and metadata conventions used in `app/`.

## Safety checks before finishing

- Verify changed routes render without runtime errors.
- Confirm imports are path-correct and dead code is not introduced.
